
Analysis Description
--------------------
Examine whether or not a codon alignment is better fit by models which
permit multiple instantaneous substitutions. v0.2 adds a separate rate
for codon-island triple-hit rates

- __Requirements__: in-frame codon alignment and a phylogenetic tree

- __Citation__: Submitted; preprint at hyphy.org/resources/fmm.pdf

- __Written by__: Sergei L Kosakovsky Pond, Sadie Wisotsky and Alexander Lucaci

- __Contact Information__: spond@temple.edu

- __Analysis Version__: 1.0


>code => Universal
>Loaded a multiple sequence alignment with **38** sequences, **330** codons, and **1** partitions from `/Users/alex/Documents/selection-tutorial/data/21-empirical/yokoyama.rh1.cds.mod.1-990.nex`
The number of omega rate classes to include in the model (permissible range = [1,10], default value = 3, integer): 
>rates => 3

>triple-islands => No


### Obtaining branch lengths and nucleotide substitution biases under the nucleotide GTR model

>kill-zero-lengths => Yes
* Log(L) = -14860.35, AIC-c = 29877.02 (78 estimated parameters)
* 1 partition. Total tree length by partition (subs/site)  3.089

### Obtaining the global omega estimate based on relative GTR branch lengths and nucleotide substitution biases
* Log(L) = -13501.81, AIC-c = 27174.80 (85 estimated parameters)
* 1 partition. Total tree length by partition (subs/site)  3.766
* non-synonymous/synonymous rate ratio for *test* =   0.1252

### Fitting Standard MG94
* Log(L) = -12819.45, AIC-c = 25820.22 (90 estimated parameters)
* non-synonymous/synonymous rate ratio =   0.1149
* The following relative rate distribution (mean 1) for site-to-site **non-synonymous** rate variation was inferred

|               Rate                | Proportion, % |               Notes               |
|-----------------------------------|---------------|-----------------------------------|
|               0.084               |    58.764     |                                   |
|               1.437               |    30.342     |                                   |
|               4.725               |    10.894     |                                   |


### Fitting MG94 with double instantaneous substitutions
* Log(L) = -12700.17, AIC-c = 25583.69 (91 estimated parameters)
* non-synonymous/synonymous rate ratio =   0.0806
* rate at which 2 nucleotides are changed instantly within a single codon =   0.7153
* The following relative rate distribution (mean 1) for site-to-site **non-synonymous** rate variation was inferred

|               Rate                | Proportion, % |               Notes               |
|-----------------------------------|---------------|-----------------------------------|
|               0.106               |    60.602     |                                   |
|               1.519               |    29.599     |                                   |
|               4.962               |     9.799     |                                   |


### Fitting MG94 with double and triple instantaneous substitutions
* Log(L) = -12689.22, AIC-c = 25563.81 (92 estimated parameters)
* non-synonymous/synonymous rate ratio =   0.0814
* rate at which 2 nucleotides are changed instantly within a single codon =   0.5527
* rate at which 3 nucleotides are changed instantly within a single codon =   0.9819
* rate at which 3 nucleotides are changed instantly within a single codon between synonymous codon islands =   0.9819
* The following relative rate distribution (mean 1) for site-to-site **non-synonymous** rate variation was inferred

|               Rate                | Proportion, % |               Notes               |
|-----------------------------------|---------------|-----------------------------------|
|               0.106               |    60.373     |                                   |
|               1.499               |    29.677     |                                   |
|               4.938               |     9.950     |                                   |


